Z||000000||Fiero-Tex||05-15-2001||05:45 PM||||I think I just need help!  I have my brakes working now, but I can't seem to get the parking brake to work correctly.  I have tried to adjust the cable from underneath the car, but it is still not holding properly.  Does anyone have any suggestions on what else I can check for?<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||KRMFiero||05-15-2001||06:01 PM||||Hmm mine does the same thing, not sure why.... i have a question about brakes though:<P>right before i started my engine conversion on my 84 I hit a rock and it ripped the front right brake line off, not the small part that goes to the caliper i took the long one that goes to the master cylinder. its broke and all bent,  where can i get a new one?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ed||05-15-2001||08:36 PM||||One area to examine is whether the mechanism is corroded.  If the parking brakes are not regularly used, they will corrode and become inoperable. Mechanism includes brake piston. <P>Everybody: Always use your parking brake. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||05-15-2001||08:50 PM||||Once you adjust the tension, You are suppose to apply the brakes (via the brake pedal) and hold them while you pump the E-brake handle to set them correctly. When I changed out my cables I had to do the above then they worked correctly. <P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">   <BR>Got Emblems?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fiero-Tex||05-16-2001||08:48 AM||||Well I know that the parking brake mechanism works.  I just replaced all of the seals on both rear calipers, and I can manually move them. I will try to apply the brake and adjust them tonight after work.<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||cadaver||05-16-2001||05:45 PM||||Most decent parts stores have brake hard lines. Just find the right size and length. Or get one out of a wrecked one if you have access.||||reg||1
